# 🍷 Wine Quality Prediction using Machine Learning

Prepared for UMBC Data Science Master Degree Capstone  
Instructor: Dr. Chaojie (Jay) Wang  
Author: Akshay Kumar Nagabandi  

---

## 📌 Project Overview

This project predicts whether a red wine sample is **Good Quality** or **Not Good Quality** using machine learning techniques and physicochemical properties of wine.

The project includes data preprocessing, exploratory data analysis (EDA), model comparison, feature importance analysis, and deployment using Streamlit.

---

## 🎯 Objective

- Predict wine quality using machine learning
- Compare multiple classification models
- Select the best-performing model
- Deploy using Streamlit for real-time prediction

---

## 📊 Dataset

**Dataset:** Red Wine Quality Dataset (Cortez et al., 2009)

**Source:**  
https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/uciml/red-wine-quality-cortez-et-al-2009

Dataset Details:

- Total Samples: 1599
- Input Features: 11
- Target Variable: Quality
- Dataset Type: Structured Numerical Dataset

---

## 📘 Target Transformation

```text
quality >= 7 → Good Quality
quality < 7 → Not Good Quality
```

---

## 🤖 Models Used

- Random Forest Classifier
- Decision Tree Classifier
- K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)

Final Selected Model:

✅ Random Forest Classifier

---

## 📊 Features Included

✔ Dataset Overview  
✔ Exploratory Data Analysis  
✔ Correlation Analysis  
✔ Feature Importance  
✔ Model Comparison  
✔ Final Model Evaluation  
✔ Real-time Prediction using Streamlit  

---

## 🛠 Technologies Used

- Python
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Scikit-Learn
- Streamlit

---

## 🚀 Run Project

Install dependencies:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

Run application:

```bash
streamlit run app.py
```

---

## ⭐ Conclusion

Random Forest achieved the highest performance among all models and was selected as the final model for predicting wine quality.

